*m: SNAP:Symbolic Nuclear Analysis Package,  Version 2.4.0, July 09, 2015
*m: PLUGIN:TRACE Version 3.4.3
*m: CODE:TRACE V 5.0 Patch 4
*m: DATE:9/23/15
*
*  The sensitivity of this model is unknown.  It was submitted by a CAMP user
*  but was not specifically identified as confidential.  Treat as proprietary for now.
*
*************
* main data *
*************
*
*       numtcr          ieos         inopt          nmat          id2o
             9             0             1             2             0
Test adjusted additive flow loss model in VESSELs at levels other than
level 1.  17 3D cell edges adjusted to match user desired flow rate.
Boundary condition is provided by two BREAK components.  Essentially
pressure drop fixed and flow loss adjusted to match desired flow rate.
Plots of interest adjusted additive flow loss contollers CB -5, -10,
-15, -20, -25, -30, -35, -40, -45, -50, -55, -60, -65, -70, -75, -80,
and -85.  Original input was changed from FILL and BREAK to two BREAKs.
Gains for control blocks listed above was changed to so that they converged
within 100 seconds.
*
*
*****************
* namelist data *
*****************
*
 &inopts
  chfmult=1000.0,
  cssMaxNumOpt=.TRUE.,
  dtstrt=-1.0,
  graphlevel="full",
  idiag=1,
  ikfac=1,
  nfrc1=2,
  nfrc3=2,
  usesjc=3,
  npower=27,
  nhtstr=27,
  nadjlosses=17
 &end
